      <article class="proj feature">
        <header>
          <h3>GLMS <small>Global Logistics Management System</small></h3>
          <span class="tag">Solo · flagship</span>
        </header>
        <p class="summary">A logistics management system built end to end in three parts: an ASP.NET Core MVC web app, a separate REST API secured with JWT bearer tokens, and a containerised build with automated tests running in CI.</p>
        <div>
          <h4>What I built</h4>
          <ul>
            <li>The MVC front end and the REST API, with JWT authentication between them.</li>
            <li>A Dockerfile that packages the solution into a reproducible image.</li>
            <li>A GitHub Actions workflow that builds the solution and runs integration tests on every push.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h4>What broke, and the fix</h4>
          <div class="log">
            <div><span class="code">401</span><span class="fix">Requests to the API came back unauthorised. Traced it to how HttpClient was scoped and fixed the client setup so the token reached the API.</span></div>
            <div><span class="code">enum</span><span class="fix">Enum values failed to deserialise between the web app and the API. Fixed the serialisation so both sides agree.</span></div>
            <div><span class="code">400</span><span class="fix">Validation rules on the client and the API disagreed. Brought them back in line.</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <footer>
          <div class="chips"><span class="chip">ASP.NET Core</span><span class="chip">C#</span><span class="chip">REST</span><span class="chip">JWT</span><span class="chip">Docker</span><span class="chip">GitHub Actions</span></div>
          <div class="stages"><span class="stage on">code</span><span class="stage on">design</span><span class="stage on">test</span><span class="stage on">ci</span><span class="stage on">container</span><span class="stage">cloud</span></div>
        </footer>
      </article>

      <article class="proj">
        <header>
          <h3>FlexiSpace <small>Boardroom Booking System</small></h3>
          <span class="tag">Team of 6 · client project</span>
        </header>
        <p class="summary">A boardroom booking platform for a real client, delivered as a Work Integrated Learning project. A .NET 8 Web API sits behind web and mobile front ends, with Microsoft Entra ID sign-in and Outlook calendar sync through the Microsoft Graph API.</p>
        <div>
          <h4>My part</h4>
          <ul>
            <li>Owned the booking logic and conflict rules that prevent double-bookings and enforce booking constraints.</li>
            <li>Contributed UML class, sequence, state and deployment diagrams for the system design.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h4>How the team shipped</h4>
          <ul>
            <li>Client-approved, Azure-only architecture: App Service for the API, Azure SQL for data, Entra ID for identity.</li>
            <li>Feature branches and pull requests, with peer review before every merge to main.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <footer>
          <div class="chips"><span class="chip">.NET 8</span><span class="chip">Web API</span><span class="chip">Entra ID</span><span class="chip">Graph API</span><span class="chip">Azure SQL</span></div>
          <div class="stages"><span class="stage on">code</span><span class="stage on">design</span><span class="stage">test</span><span class="stage">ci</span><span class="stage">container</span><span class="stage on">cloud</span></div>
        </footer>
      </article>

      <article class="proj compact">
